  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"2.18.5\"\n\npackage:\n  name: mycli\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/m/mycli/mycli-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: d6891c252d4068607e6bdac59c0b4ea7573d4e0a69c54420c18e0fcd98fecfd8\n  patches:\n    # zsh prints `NAME=value` for a `typeset NAME` of an already-exported\n    # parameter, and conda always exports PREFIX, so the zsh completion test\n    # harness emits a stray line and fails wherever zsh is installed. Not yet\n    # submitted upstream.\n    - patches/0001-initialise-zsh-completion-harness-locals.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n  python:\n    entry_points:\n      - mycli = mycli.main:main\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - pip\n    - setuptools >=64.0\n    - setuptools-scm >=8\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - click >=8.3.3,<8.4.0\n    - clickdc >=0.1.1,<0.2.0\n    - cryptography >=50.0.0,<50.1.0\n    - pygments >=2.21.0,<2.22.0\n    - prompt_toolkit >=3.0.41,<4.0.0\n    - pymysql >=1.1.2,<1.2.0\n    - sqlparse >=0.3.0,<0.6.0\n    - sqlglot >=30.17.0,<30.18.0\n    - sqlglotc >=30.17.0,<30.18.0\n    - configobj >=5.0.9,<5.1.0\n    - cli_helpers >=2.15.1,<2.16.0\n    - wcwidth >=0.8.2,<0.9.0\n    - pyperclip >=1.11.0,<1.12.0\n    - pycryptodomex >=3.23.0,<3.24.0\n    - pyfzf >=0.3.1,<0.4.0\n    - rapidfuzz >=3.14.3,<3.15.0\n    - keyring >=25.7.0,<25.8.0\n    - jinja2 >=3.1.6,<3.2.0\n    - yaspin >=3.4.0,<3.5.0\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - mycli\n        - mycli.main\n        - mycli.packages\n        - mycli.packages.ptoolkit\n        - mycli.packages.special\n        - mycli.packages.tabular_output\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n      pip_check: true\n  - script:\n      # mycli.main imports the whole dependency stack at module level, so this\n      # also proves every run dependency resolves and loads.\n      - mycli --help\n      # Upstream's unit tests. Run as `python -m` so the sdist root is on\n      # sys.path for `test.utils`; the tests needing a live MySQL skip\n      # themselves through that module's dbtest marker. The ignored modules\n      # cover the `dataframe` and `llm` extras, which this package does not\n      # ship.\n      - python -m pytest test/pytests -v\n        --ignore=test/pytests/test_polars_completion.py\n        --ignore=test/pytests/test_polars_transform.py\n        --ignore=test/pytests/test_special_llm.py\n    files:\n      source:\n        - test/\n        # The completion tests compare `mycli --completions <shell>` against\n        # these checked-in scripts, found relative to the sdist root.\n        - mycli/resources/completions/\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - pytest\n        - pexpect\n        - packaging\n  - package_contents:\n      strict: true\n      site_packages:\n        - mycli\n        - mycli.packages\n        - mycli.packages.ptoolkit\n        - mycli.packages.special\n        - mycli.packages.tabular_output\n      files:\n        # Directory globs, so new modules and completion scripts are absorbed\n        # while strict still catches anything landing outside site-packages.\n        - site-packages/mycli/**\n        - site-packages/mycli-${{ version }}.dist-info/**\n        - etc/conda/test-files/mycli/**\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://mycli.net\n  summary: Rich MySQL terminal client with autocompletion, syntax highlighting, and dataframes\n  description: |\n    mycli is a command line interface for MySQL, MariaDB and Percona with\n    auto-completion and syntax highlighting. It completes table names, columns\n    and keywords as you type, highlights the query, and renders results in a\n    range of tabular formats.\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE.txt\n  repository: https://github.com/dbcli/mycli\n  documentation: https://www.mycli.net/docs\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - tschoonj\n",
